 {"id": "OPS-009", "title": "P1 - scheduler namespace S3 push FAILS: remote holds TWO refs/heads/master -> dst refspec matches more than one, off-box mirror stale", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 3, "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "reasoning": "Watchdog scan 2026-09-18 16:00Z. duckbrain-http daemon journal (node pid 2229147, service start 2026-09-18T05:19Z) at 16:03:45Z: \"error: dst refspec refs/heads/master matches more than one\" + \"error: failed to push some refs to s3://duckbrain/current/git/scheduler\". Root cause proved read-only: git ls-remote s3daily in duckbrain/namespaces/scheduler returns TWO refs/heads/master with different SHAs (fabd19fadc8c9d0097b0c646e436e529997b34ad AND dffe583421dd0bc36ff4d7bc6c47f3c1e4b7f7c4) plus a stray refs/heads/master_supfix0911 -> the dst refspec is ambiguous, so every git-remote-s3 push for this namespace is refused. Blast radius = scheduler namespace ONLY: coding-hermes, bankai and trouble each return exactly one HEAD+refs/heads/master. Consequence: the namespace auto-commit mirror to S3 never lands; scheduler namespace data exists only on local disk. Fix (duckbrain): dedupe the stale master bundle/ref in the S3 git store (or re-init the remote path) then re-push; verify with git ls-remote returning a single master.", "capability_tags": [], "created_at": "2026-09-18T16:07:50Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-18T16:07:50Z", "worker_status": "complete", "completed_at": "2026-09-18T17:44:39.728417+00:00", "commit_hash": "0cf3dd2", "files_changed": [], "lines_added": 0, "lines_removed": 0, "guard_result": "PASS (gitreins tier1 secrets+tests; tier2 6bb8ebbd COMPLETE)", "ci_result": "single batched-push run on 3e34a45 (aff56d2+0cf3dd2+3e34a45 pushed together) = SUCCESS (17:47Z queued, 12:50:35 local completed)", "worker_summary": "foreman-direct ops (no worker): quarantined the stale duplicate refs/heads/master bundle for scheduler/default/hermes-canopy (size-verified, reversible), removed the stray master_supfix