 {"id": "S3-GIT-005", "title": "P3 - duplicate-bundle harness can silently run fewer assertions (51/0 vs 43/0 across four runs, all green) - add a per-case run/skip ledger", "status": "complete", "priority": "P3", "complexity": 1, "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "reasoning": "Found while closing S3-GIT-004 (tick 529). scripts/s3/test-duplicate-bundle-repair.sh (the new hermetic duplicate-bundle harness) reported 51 passed / 0 failed in the foreman's two runs AND in the S3-GIT-004 tier-2 judge's run, but the OPS-009 tier-2 judge's independent run of the SAME harness printed 43 passed / 0 failed - 8 assertions fewer with zero failures. All four runs exited 0. The likely mechanism is a case being skipped in that environment (case E depends on detecting a git-remote-s3 helper process, which is host-activity dependent), but the harness has no ledger that says which cases ran, so the delta cannot be attributed after the fact. That is the phantom-pass anti-pattern in miniature: a gate whose coverage silently shrinks with host state still reads green. FIX: make the harness print a per-case ledger (case id, assertions run, PASS/FAIL/SKIP) and exit non-zero (or at minimum loudly mark the run PARTIAL) when any case did not run its full assertion set, so a green line always means the same set of assertions executed. ACCEPTANCE: (a) a normal run prints the six case lines plus a total; (b) a run with a case forced to skip reports the skip explicitly and does not print a bare '51 passed'; (c) the four-run count delta becomes self-explaining from the output alone. Shell only - no vitest/TS files (CI asserts the AGENTS.md counts).", "capability_tags": [], "source": "foreman:tick-529 (observed while closing S3-GIT-004)", "created_at": "2026-09-18T17:51:05Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-18T18:10:33.002169+00:00", "created_by": "foreman:tick-529", "worker_status": "complete", "completed_at": "2026-09-18T18:10:33.002169+00:00", "commit_hash": "ca257e5", "files_changed": ["scripts/s3/test-duplicate-bundle-repair.sh", "scripts/s3/README.md"], "lines_added": 235, "lines_removed": 1, "guard_result": "PASS (gitreins tier1 secrets+tests; tier2 d202eb73 COMPLETE) + foreman-independent controls: normal rc=0 ledger 7/7 51/51, forced-skip rc=3 43 PASS no green line, dropped-assertion and removed-case controls both rc=3", "ci_result": "GREEN — single batched-push run on the pushed HEAD 27bc426 (ca257e5 work + 179dee6 gitreins records + 27bc426 board closeout pushed together) completed/success (18:11:14Z queued, 2026-09-18T18:14:04Z local completed); the previous tick's runs are all success too — no red run to file", "worker_summary": "k3@kimi-for-coding (1 dispatch, exit 0, committed ca257e5): added a per-case ledger (case_begin/case_end, per-case assertion counts, PASS/FAIL/SKIP) plus a declared ROSTER (A17 B6 C4 D6 E5 F5 G8) and a roster contract to scripts/s3/test-duplicate-bundle-repair.sh; an incomplete run now prints SKIP/PARTIAL + 'harness: INCOMPLETE ... exit 3' and never the clean green line; test-only DUCKBRAIN_S3_HARNESS_SKIP_CASE hook proves it without editing the script; README documents the ledger, the exit-code table and the contract. Assertions untouched (0 added, 0 removed, 0 reworded).", "foreman_note": "Root cause CORRECTED by this tick's recon: the 43-assertion run was NOT a host-dependent skip of case E. 17+6+4+6+5+5 = 43 exactly, i.e. that run was missing case G (8 assertions) - a judge that ran an in-flight/pre-case-G working-tree copy before the script was finished (aff56d2 already contains all 7 cases, and the harness has exactly one commit). Case E's guard is untouched and passed in every run. The delta is now self-explaining from the output alone, which is what the row asked for."}
